  <layout>Printed page with a running title-less top: page number at top left, then three tree diagrams (Tabulae XXVII, XXIIX, XXIX) in the main block, one under the other. No margin notes.</layout>
  <page_number>752</page_number>
  <main_text>
    <head level="1" caput="27">TABVLA XXVII.</head>
    <l type="diagram" level="1">Viles &amp; sordidæ Artes sunt vel</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="2">[?]riaria; Coquæ vel</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Præparans: vt ars alutariorum alborum &amp; rubrorum, vt vulgo distinguuntur,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Conficiens: vt</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Sutoria,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Pellionum &amp;c.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Ephippiaria.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="2">Purgatoria quæuis: vt, Balneatorum, barbitonsorum, &amp; aliorum huius generis.</l>
    <head level="1" caput="28">TABVLA XXIIX.</head>
    <l type="diagram" level="1">Viuendi</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="2">Decoræ, vt est ars</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Pictoria, seu acu, seu calamo &amp; penicillo.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Cælatoria,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Sculptoria.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="2">Iucunde: vt ars</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Cantoria</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Vocalis,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Instrumentalis.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Saltatoria,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Histrionica,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Cupedinaria,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Lusoria per pilam, &amp; alia eiusmodi exercitamenta palæstrica.</l>
    <head level="1" caput="29">TABVLA XXIX.</head>
    <l type="diagram" level="1">Actualis qualitas est vel</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="2">Afficiens (scilicet sensus, seu patibilis, vel</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Prima: eaque vel</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Magis efficax: vt</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Lux,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Frigus,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Calor.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Minus efficax: vt</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Humiditas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Siccitas.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Secunda, seu orta à primis: idq; vel</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Propinquæ: vt</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Raritas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Densitas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Leuitas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Grauitas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Mollities,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Duritics,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Lævitas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Asperitas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Lubricitas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Viscositas &amp; Lentor,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Friabilitas,</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="5">Ariditas.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Remotæ: vt Vide Tab. [?]</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="2">Conformans, &amp; dicitur Forma ac Figura, quæ vel</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Naturalis in corporibus</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Imperfectis: vt Meteora non pauca: Chasmata, iris, fossæ, parelia, &amp;c.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="4">Perfectis: vt figuræ plantarum, animalium.</l>
    <l type="diagram" level="3">Artificialis: vt figura vestis, sellæ, mensæ, gladii, &amp;c.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Tabula XXIIX is printed "XXIIX" in the scan. Diagram labels at the far right edge are cut off. "TAL" at the lower right margin is a cropped fragment of a running or signature word and is not transcribed. The "Coquæ" and "Remotæ ... Tab. [?]" readings are uncertain. The pale show-through text of the reverse page is not transcribed.</notes>
</page>
